# Manyhalls scratch reaper — one sweep (Proofdelve ForgeOs-nv0j, the durable half of
# incident Proofdelve ForgeOs-7gag; Proofdelve ForgeOs-mpaw's worktree half). Drafted under Regent
# edict 2026-09-12, gate 6, the Overseer's signature recorded on the bead;
# installed by hand into ~/.config/systemd/user/ — this file does nothing where
# it lives in the repo.
#
# Each firing runs fort/scripts/scratch-reaper.sh once. Its header is the
# design; in one line: remove Warden scratch copies older than two hours whose
# review lock nobody holds (what a SIGKILL leaves, since warden.sh removes its
# own copy on exit), and remove bead worktrees that stranded-sweep.sh --reapable
# lists (merged into main, bead closed) when the tree is clean and no launcher
# holds its .forge.lock -- branch and worktree together, or neither.
#
# WHY A TIMER AND NOT tmpfiles.d: tmpfiles runs daily, and on 2026-09-12 the
# Warden's litter filled the 12764M /tmp quota inside one working day and took a
# Warden, the host verifier and two Forges down in the same second. Hourly is
# the cadence a busy day needs; the age floor inside the script is what keeps
# an hourly sweep from touching anything a review could still want.
#
# It reads nothing of the fleet's state and never touches the halt file. It
# exits 1 when a removal FAILED (the unit then shows in --failed, which is the
# point: a reaper that cannot reap is a disk that keeps filling) and 64 when the
# worktree list could not be obtained.

[Unit]
Description=Manyhalls scratch reaper — Warden scratch and merged bead worktrees

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/home/justin/dev/fortkit
# User units do not inherit a login shell PATH. bd lives in ~/.local/bin and
# stranded-sweep.sh asks it per candidate; git, flock and jq are in /usr/bin.
Environment=PATH=/home/justin/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
ExecStart=/home/justin/dev/fortkit/fort/scripts/scratch-reaper.sh
# stranded-sweep.sh asks bd ONCE, via a single `bd export`, and answers every
# branch and worktree from that snapshot (Proofdelve ForgeOs-56d6.1). It used to run one
# `bd show` per branch, which is what this comment said until 2026-09-23 and
# what made a session-start sweep take 7m09s against 385 branches; the timeout
# below was sized for that shape and is left generous on purpose.
#
# A sweep is normally well under a minute. Anything longer is bd hanging, and a
# hung reaper must not sit on the next hour.
TimeoutStartSec=15min
